1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,082
Hand someone a thousand-dollar paycheck and

2
00:00:03,082 --> 00:00:04,658
they guard every cent.

3
00:00:04,658 --> 00:00:07,453
Hand that same person a thousand-dollar

4
00:00:07,453 --> 00:00:09,173
tax refund and it is far

5
00:00:09,173 --> 00:00:10,320
easier to spend.

6
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:13,044
Economist Richard Thaler won the 2017

7
00:00:13,044 --> 00:00:13,927
Nobel Prize,

8
00:00:13,927 --> 00:00:15,988
in part for describing this.

9
00:00:15,988 --> 00:00:18,270
He called it mental accounting.

10
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:20,111
Money is interchangeable,

11
00:00:20,111 --> 00:00:22,466
but your brain tags every dollar

12
00:00:22,466 --> 00:00:24,454
with a story about where it

13
00:00:24,454 --> 00:00:25,190
came from.

14
00:00:25,190 --> 00:00:27,727
Salary dollars feel heavy because you

15
00:00:27,727 --> 00:00:29,852
traded forty hours of stress to

16
00:00:29,852 --> 00:00:30,538
earn them.

17
00:00:30,538 --> 00:00:33,280
Refund or bonus dollars feel weightless,

18
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:34,446
like house money,

19
00:00:34,446 --> 00:00:36,640
so spending friction disappears.

20
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,553
Use the Fungibility Rule:

21
00:00:38,553 --> 00:00:39,854
park every bonus,

22
00:00:39,854 --> 00:00:40,236
gift,

23
00:00:40,236 --> 00:00:42,379
or tax refund in savings for

24
00:00:42,379 --> 00:00:45,210
fourteen days until the windfall rush

25
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:45,669
fades.

26
00:00:45,669 --> 00:00:47,582
Then ask if you would buy

27
00:00:47,582 --> 00:00:50,030
that upgrade using overtime pay.

28
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:52,094
Once you strip the fake label

29
00:00:52,094 --> 00:00:53,090
off your cash,

30
00:00:53,090 --> 00:00:56,720
every windfall starts compounding like real wealth.
